%N A399598 Table A(n,m) read by upward antidiagonals such that A(n,m) is the smallest number prime(i+n-1)^m * Product_{j=i..i+n-1} prime(j) such that log(prime(i+n-1)) / log(prime(i)) <= (m+1)/m with i>0.
%C A399598 Let rad(k) = A007947(k) be the squarefree kernel of k.
%C A399598 Table A(n,m) read by diagonals: A(n,m) is the smallest number of the form p_n^m * rad(A(n,m)) such that A008479(A(n,m)) = binomial(n+m, m) = A014410(n,m), where p_i is the i-th smallest distinct prime factor of k.
